<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bayer</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bayer is a German chemical and pharmaceutical company founded in the nineteenth century. Along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basf">BASF</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hoechst">Hoechst</a>, it led the chemical industry of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>, which by 1913 dominated the global market for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/synthetic-dye">synthetic dyes</a>. The company exemplifies the science-based industrial growth that made <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> the largest economy in continental <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bayer.jpg" alt="Bayer" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bayer AG · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Logo_Bayer.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
